.SH BUGS
This is an experimental privileged interface, not an OpenGL implementation.
It supports one GPU, 32 contexts, 4096 resources and 256 MiB of backing per context.
Each resource's backing store is limited to 64 MiB.
There is one control queue with at most one outstanding request.
Cursor queues, exported DMA buffers and device recovery are not implemented.
The display uses a separate backing allocation of up to 64 MiB.
.PP
Resource targets are 0 through 8. Buffers are limited to 64 MiB;
texture dimensions to 16384, array size to 2048, highest mip level to 14,
and sample count to 64. The host may impose lower limits.
Backing size and transfer layout must match the resource format.
Guest backing limits do not bound the host GPU memory consumed by a resource.
.PP
QEMU does not propagate all VirGL renderer errors to the guest.
A successful fence confirms transport completion, not a valid rendering result.
